Hello Harry,

All of the modules within MSc Smart Agriculture are considered core modules and are essential to the learning outcomes of the course. Because of this, we would not be able to switch out the ARES40380 Sustainability in the Food Supply Chain module, especially not for modules on other courses.

While you haven't disclosed your reasons for not looking forward to this module, it would be advisable to speak with the module leader Hannah Ronan-Brown, who can cover the module structure in greater detail and hopefully remedy any apprehension.

Kind regards,

Kevin Bowers
Subject Coordinator
School of Animal, Rural and Environmental Sciences
E: kevin.bowers@ntu.ac.uk<mailto:kevin.bowers@ntu.ac.uk>

From: Harry Wright 2016 (N0605150) <harry.wright2016@my.ntu.ac.uk>
Sent: 03 January 2026 17:06
To: ARE Admin <AREAdmin@ntu.ac.uk>
Subject: Module Change

I'm a PT student and need to complete one more module (excluding my dissertation) to complete my MSc.

Is there any way to change my remaining module that I start in January?  I'm not looking forward to completing my remaining one.
These look promising from Applied Ecology and Geospatial Techniques MRes; MSc


Remote Sensing and Advanced Geographical Information Systems
Obtain and utilise existing remote sensing data to enhance research in ecology and conservation. This module will also give you the skills and experience to operate and collect information from a range of recent and emerging geospatial technologies.
20 credits
Or alternatively

Geographical Information Systems (GIS)
GIS is an important tool for monitoring biodiversity and can be used to store, manipulate, analyse and present large amounts of spatial and attribute data - data that can be used to target surveys and monitoring schemes. Data collected during field surveys and from remotely sensed images taken into GIS allow the monitoring of both the location and extent of change. In this module, you'll explore the application of GIS and Global Navigation Satellite Systems (GNSS) technology within biodiversity conservation.
20 credits

These seem more relevant to my skillset. I don't know what's running at the moment...

Harry Wright (N0605150)
Smart Agriculture PT Year 2

